What the hell is that angle?

2186
02:21:26,430 --> 02:21:28,770
Oh, I'm not in an equatorial orbit.

2187
02:21:28,770 --> 02:21:29,290
That makes sense.

2188
02:21:30,330 --> 02:21:31,330
Let's bring it down slightly.

2189
02:21:35,590 --> 02:21:36,530
Oh, that's too much.

2190
02:21:36,530 --> 02:21:36,930
I see.

2191
02:21:48,510 --> 02:21:49,490
Let's do 30.

2192
02:21:49,810 --> 02:21:50,350
36.

2193
02:21:52,310 --> 02:21:53,430
That's nine days.

2194
02:21:56,010 --> 02:21:57,930
We're actually going to come back around, it seems.

2195
02:22:02,830 --> 02:22:05,030
Assuming we make it through the atmosphere, but we're not.

2196
02:22:06,650 --> 02:22:07,770
This should work, right?

2197
02:22:08,850 --> 02:22:10,750
Okay, let's just do this.

2198
02:22:13,230 --> 02:22:14,070
35 minutes.

2199
02:22:21,870 --> 02:22:25,770
Electric charges... Dude, I was worried about solar panels.

2200
02:22:25,930 --> 02:22:26,510
Come on.

2201
02:22:27,350 --> 02:22:28,670
There's no need for that.

2202
02:22:29,050 --> 02:22:30,630
Not when you got a poodle.

2203
02:22:39,230 --> 02:22:41,170
Now we align ourselves accordingly.

2204
02:22:45,750 --> 02:22:46,870
Right there.

2205
02:23:10,430 --> 02:23:13,150
Dude, I can't tell with these extra frickin' thingies.

2206
02:23:14,770 --> 02:23:16,370
Let me burn prograde slightly.

2207
02:23:16,650 --> 02:23:17,110
I mean retro.

2208
02:23:28,950 --> 02:23:29,470
37.

2209
02:23:29,470 --> 02:23:30,290
We got it.

2210
02:23:31,550 --> 02:23:32,250
And that's it.

2211
02:23:33,610 --> 02:23:34,630
We're going home.

2212
02:23:35,290 --> 02:23:38,290
I'm gonna set a... fast forward point.

2213
02:23:38,810 --> 02:23:40,250
Actually a maneuver just to be safe.

2214
02:23:41,870 --> 02:23:42,690
Should we trust?

2215
02:23:42,850 --> 02:23:43,570
Should we trust on this?

2216
02:23:44,010 --> 02:23:46,430
I'm ready to cancel time warp if we don't trust.

2217
02:23:47,250 --> 02:23:48,730
I'm gonna put it right here.

2218
02:23:53,040 --> 02:23:53,640
Warp.

2219
02:23:53,640 --> 02:23:54,600
Wish me luck!

2220
02:23:55,060 --> 02:23:56,420
Bye-bye, Minmus!

2221
02:24:00,340 --> 02:24:01,180
Where's Kerbin?

2222
02:24:05,600 --> 02:24:06,600
Oh, there it is.

2223
02:24:10,860 --> 02:24:11,840
We're coming home.

2224
02:24:14,700 --> 02:24:18,340
Was that the shadow of the moon just going across the surface there?

2225
02:24:19,180 --> 02:24:20,020
That was sick.

2226
02:24:22,360 --> 02:24:22,860
Oh!

2227
02:24:24,540 --> 02:24:26,020
Service deployed mystery goo observations.

2228
02:24:26,280 --> 02:24:27,060
Can I see that here?

2229
02:24:28,320 --> 02:24:32,260
I wish I could see the... So it's kind of fast now, man.

2230
02:24:32,260 --> 02:24:32,900
It's collecting.

2231
02:24:34,180 --> 02:24:35,040
Very nice.

2232
02:24:44,180 --> 02:24:44,840
Here we come.

2233
02:24:47,880 --> 02:24:49,860
Ah, we're gonna be on the dark side.

2234
02:24:50,400 --> 02:24:51,240
Do I like that?

2235
02:24:52,820 --> 02:24:53,340
That's okay.

2236
02:24:55,060 --> 02:24:57,640
In fact, I can already disengage the last... Look at this.

2237
02:24:57,740 --> 02:24:58,760
A thousand delta V.

2238
02:24:58,840 --> 02:25:00,000
We don't even need it, baby.

2239
02:25:01,200 --> 02:25:02,500
In fact, I'm gonna get rid of it now.

2240
02:25:06,880 --> 02:25:07,780
I'm getting rid of it now.

2241
02:25:17,360 --> 02:25:18,520
Oh, that's naughty.

2242
02:25:19,020 --> 02:25:20,080
That's very naughty.

2243
02:25:26,780 --> 02:25:27,940
Here we go.

2244
02:25:30,740 --> 02:25:31,600
Come on.

2245
02:25:46,020 --> 02:25:47,740
It's gonna be a night landing, but that's alright.

2246
02:25:55,260 --> 02:25:56,040
Angle yourself.

2247
02:26:00,280 --> 02:26:01,160
280 kilometers.

2248
02:26:01,340 --> 02:26:02,000
Okay, there's still time.

2249
02:26:05,820 --> 02:26:06,860
Here we go, here we go.

2250
02:26:08,420 --> 02:26:08,940
Hundred.

2251
02:26:10,500 --> 02:26:11,020
Eighty.

2252
02:26:11,680 --> 02:26:12,200
Seventy.

2253
02:26:12,340 --> 02:26:12,860
We're in the atmosphere.

2254
02:26:14,180 --> 02:26:14,980
All right, guys.

2255
02:26:15,980 --> 02:26:18,740
We're coming home with Frohat and all the science.

2256
02:26:19,060 --> 02:26:21,540
Or all the objectives done, I guess.

2257
02:26:24,180 --> 02:26:25,060
Let's do this.

2258
02:26:28,840 --> 02:26:29,800
Looks good, yo.

2259
02:26:33,040 --> 02:26:34,300
Looks real good.

2260
02:26:38,260 --> 02:26:39,320
What's that over there?

2261
02:26:39,820 --> 02:26:41,080
Universal rocket debris.

2262
02:26:41,360 --> 02:26:42,260
Oh, that burned up.

2263
02:26:46,300 --> 02:26:48,280
Come on, show me some sun before I land.

2264
02:26:49,580 --> 02:26:50,700
Give me a taste.

2265
02:26:53,520 --> 02:26:54,480
Just a taste.

2266
02:26:55,460 --> 02:26:57,360
Don't make me land in the dark.

2267
02:27:01,180 --> 02:27:03,260
A cheeky sunrise for the boys?

2268
02:27:14,700 --> 02:27:16,240
Doesn't look like we're gonna get a sunrise.

2269
02:27:17,120 --> 02:27:17,860
That's okay, though.

2270
02:27:19,700 --> 02:27:20,860
We seem to be over land.

2271
02:27:25,720 --> 02:27:26,680
Yep.

2272
02:27:28,260 --> 02:27:29,760
Keep slowing down.

2273
02:27:31,940 --> 02:27:33,380
And shoots.

2274
02:27:36,060 --> 02:27:37,440
SAS off.

2275
02:27:38,280 --> 02:27:39,940
Hold on to your hats and goggles.

2276
02:27:40,660 --> 02:27:42,360
Especially your hat, frohat.

2277
02:27:47,680 --> 02:27:48,900
Coming down.

2278
02:27:52,660 --> 02:27:56,420
Parachute deploy in 2... 1... Now.

2279
02:27:57,680 --> 02:28:00,100
Oh, we're really... Why are we so fast?

2280
02:28:01,980 --> 02:28:03,120
Okay, there we go, there we go.

2281
02:28:04,040 --> 02:28:05,800
In fact, I'm gonna disengage this.

2282
02:28:07,560 --> 02:28:08,380
Bye-bye.

2283
02:28:13,600 --> 02:28:14,220
Nice.

2284
02:28:18,360 --> 02:28:18,980
Guys?

2285
02:28:19,480 --> 02:28:20,660
Have we done it?

2286
02:28:27,000 --> 02:28:30,340
The believers are awarded again.

2287
02:28:33,080 --> 02:28:34,480
Boom!

2288
02:28:37,800 --> 02:28:38,380
Wow.

2289
02:28:39,560 --> 02:28:41,320
Wow, what a mission.

2290
02:28:41,980 --> 02:28:43,600
Holy shit, that was fun.

2291
02:28:44,280 --> 02:28:46,280
We even got seven signs out of it somehow.

2292
02:28:47,120 --> 02:28:49,300
Look at this XP, XP, XP.

2293
02:28:49,460 --> 02:28:50,720
Everyone's getting so much experience.

2294
02:28:51,440 --> 02:28:53,540
We got almost a million in the bank.

2295
02:28:53,880 --> 02:28:54,920
Oh, man.

2296
02:28:55,460 --> 02:28:55,900
But hold on.

2297
02:28:56,360 --> 02:28:58,920
We actually collected some mystery goo, it said.

2298
02:28:59,940 --> 02:29:00,900
Let me see that.

2299
02:29:03,660 --> 02:29:04,240
Neildon.

2300
02:29:09,600 --> 02:29:11,060
Let me see what's going on here.

2301
02:29:13,080 --> 02:29:14,520
Mystery goo is there.

2302
02:29:15,840 --> 02:29:18,480
Oh, I... He doesn't have a jetpack!

2303
02:29:21,020 --> 02:29:23,320
I must... Oh, shit, this guy doesn't have a jetpack either.

2304
02:29:24,360 --> 02:29:25,960
I didn't leave him any jetpacks.

2305
02:29:27,900 --> 02:29:29,800
Whoa, 16% already!

2306
02:29:33,100 --> 02:29:35,800
Wait, this is much faster than the last time I did this.

2307
02:29:37,080 --> 02:29:37,480
Yeah!

2308
02:29:38,140 --> 02:29:39,040
Let me go see this thing.

2309
02:29:39,400 --> 02:29:40,740
I can't believe nothing happened.

2310
02:29:45,620 --> 02:29:45,940
0%.

2311
02:29:45,940 --> 02:29:47,480
Science rate is 45%.

2312
02:29:47,480 --> 02:29:51,460
Maybe I need to do it closer or something.

2313
02:29:53,100 --> 02:29:53,700
I don't know.

2314
02:29:54,660 --> 02:29:56,020
I think I was too far away with it.

2315
02:29:56,920 --> 02:30:00,680
Or maybe we need to, like, impact even faster, right?

2316
02:30:02,240 --> 02:30:04,620
Okay, let's see if we can scrounge up a jetpack for you.

2317
02:30:08,200 --> 02:30:09,280
Is there a jetpack in here?

2318
02:30:10,080 --> 02:30:11,260
Oh, there is!

2319
02:30:11,580 --> 02:30:12,700
How lovely is that?

2320
02:30:13,000 --> 02:30:14,140
We're even gonna get this.

2321
02:30:15,600 --> 02:30:18,580
And we also had another Kerbal here that needed a jetpack.

2322
02:30:27,460 --> 02:30:28,140
Let's see here.

2323
02:30:29,060 --> 02:30:29,620
Oh, wait, no.

2324
02:30:32,240 --> 02:30:32,600
Nice.

2325
02:30:32,940 --> 02:30:37,000
Oh, wait, that is... No, that's Gildrin.

2326
02:30:37,120 --> 02:30:37,300
Okay.

2327
02:30:38,240 --> 02:30:39,640
Wait, there's a Gildrin in here?

2328
02:30:41,060 --> 02:30:42,360
I forgot about this guy.

2329
02:30:44,220 --> 02:30:46,040
I had no idea we had a Kerbal in there.

2330
02:30:46,800 --> 02:30:47,480
Well, there you go.

2331
02:30:49,200 --> 02:30:51,620
In fact, I'm going to give you more juice for your pack.

2332
02:30:53,460 --> 02:30:53,820
Gildrin.

2333
02:30:55,710 --> 02:30:56,690
Frickin' Gilderun dude.

2334
02:30:59,170 --> 02:31:02,070
Okay, well, at least this one is, uh, that one is working now.

2335
02:31:02,410 --> 02:31:03,690
So we just gotta wait a little bit.

2336
02:31:03,790 --> 02:31:05,850
And it didn't seem like it's gonna take long, right?

2337
02:31:06,310 --> 02:31:09,230
Because even on our journey back, we already have this much.

2338
02:31:09,850 --> 02:31:10,870
16.7.

2339
02:31:11,450 --> 02:31:12,110
Not bad.

2340
02:31:13,670 --> 02:31:14,270
Space Center.

2341
02:31:19,510 --> 02:31:22,070
Okay, so now I'm gonna go crack open the cold one.

2342
02:31:22,190 --> 02:31:24,010
It's been in the fridge long enough now, I think.

2343
02:31:24,830 --> 02:31:25,710
Quick break here.

2344
02:31:25,970 --> 02:31:27,710
I'll be back in like five minutes, okay?

2345
02:31:28,490 --> 02:31:29,050
Good luck.

2346
02:36:34,960 --> 02:36:39,080
Man, that calls for a... You know what I mean?

2347
02:36:40,300 --> 02:36:42,080
That calls for a celebration.

2348
02:36:42,500 --> 02:36:44,240
What a mission that was.

2349
02:36:44,620 --> 02:36:44,800
Wow.

2350
02:36:46,000 --> 02:36:47,160
Doubters and shambles.

2351
02:36:48,380 --> 02:36:49,160
Love to see it.

2352
02:37:05,560 --> 02:37:06,480
Let's go.

2353
02:37:14,160 --> 02:37:15,260
Alright, what's next?

2354
02:37:15,600 --> 02:37:16,940
We got money in the bank.

2355
02:37:17,300 --> 02:37:18,820
We got no science.

2356
02:37:19,020 --> 02:37:19,660
At all.

2357
02:37:20,920 --> 02:37:21,700
That's okay, though.

2358
02:37:22,860 --> 02:37:24,140
Build a new station around the moon?

2359
02:37:24,220 --> 02:37:24,720
Come on, brother.

2360
02:37:24,900 --> 02:37:25,540
I'm not doing that.

2361
02:37:27,180 --> 02:37:28,740
Seismic surveys of Eve.

2362
02:37:28,980 --> 02:37:30,000
That sounds difficult.

2363
02:37:32,400 --> 02:37:34,440
A complex scan with a rover arm.

2364
02:37:35,380 --> 02:37:36,140
Sounds difficult.

2365
02:37:37,180 --> 02:37:38,600
Wait, a baobab tree?

2366
02:37:43,440 --> 02:37:46,780
Transmix... transmits six, seven percent of the total available science.

2367
02:37:47,140 --> 02:37:47,420
Okay.

2368
02:37:49,480 --> 02:37:49,880
Sure.

2369
02:37:50,720 --> 02:37:51,440
Explore Gilly?

2370
02:37:52,260 --> 02:37:53,040
Come on, brother.

2371
02:37:55,460 --> 02:37:58,740
Docking on or around Gilly is a stepping stone to building greater things.

2372
02:37:59,680 --> 02:38:01,420
I want to go to Doona, though.

2373
02:38:04,640 --> 02:38:05,880
Plant a flag on the moon.

2374
02:38:06,000 --> 02:38:07,420
Wait, don't we have people on the moon right now?

2375
02:38:07,640 --> 02:38:08,440
Wouldn't that be an easy one?

2376
02:38:09,260 --> 02:38:10,620
Do we actually have people on the moon?

2377
02:38:13,760 --> 02:38:14,860
Mun, mun, mun, mun, mun.

2378
02:38:18,150 --> 02:38:22,830
Something about... landed at... Minmus.

2379
02:38:24,430 --> 02:38:25,930
We have no people on the moon?

2380
02:38:27,610 --> 02:38:28,550
That's actually crazy.

2381
02:38:30,610 --> 02:38:31,010
Huh.

2382
02:38:32,070 --> 02:38:32,850
The more you know.

2383
02:38:33,470 --> 02:38:35,150
I could have sworn we had at least a couple.

2384
02:38:37,590 --> 02:38:37,990
Alright.

2385
02:38:38,310 --> 02:38:39,030
Wait, not that one.

2386
02:38:41,570 --> 02:38:42,570
Temperature surveys of Eve.

2387
02:38:42,610 --> 02:38:43,590
I don't care about Eve!

2388
02:38:43,710 --> 02:38:44,770
I mean, I do care, but...

2389
02:38:44,860 --> 02:38:46,420
I wanna go another place, please.

2390
02:38:47,020 --> 02:38:49,020
Can you give me a contract for that?

2391
02:38:51,620 --> 02:38:52,500
You know what?

2392
02:38:53,080 --> 02:38:55,080
I am gonna go to Duna.

2393
02:38:55,380 --> 02:38:56,760
What's the current alignment?

2394
02:38:58,700 --> 02:39:01,040
So Duna was like 44 degrees, I think.

2395
02:39:02,520 --> 02:39:04,400
I mean, we're catching up to Duna pretty soon.

2396
02:39:06,480 --> 02:39:07,040
Yeah.

2397
02:39:08,360 --> 02:39:09,560
Not that bad, actually.

2398
02:39:11,200 --> 02:39:11,520
Yep.

2399
02:39:12,980 --> 02:39:13,540
Beautiful.

2400
02:39:16,900 --> 02:39:18,140
Let's make a Duna rocket!

2401
02:39:23,920 --> 02:39:27,900
I'm just gonna start off with my Eever.

2402
02:39:28,240 --> 02:39:28,920
My Eve.

2403
02:39:31,220 --> 02:39:32,420
We're doing the same thing.

2404
02:39:33,540 --> 02:39:35,960
This one has an absurd amount of Delta V.

2405
02:39:36,060 --> 02:39:37,140
I mean, would you look at that.

2406
02:39:37,680 --> 02:39:39,320
That is beautiful, isn't it?

2407
02:39:40,300 --> 02:39:42,780
And hold on, we just got some new rover legs, didn't we?

2408
02:39:43,040 --> 02:39:44,060
Rover legs.

2409
02:39:44,360 --> 02:39:46,340
I mean, rover wheels.

2410
02:39:47,900 --> 02:39:53,080
So how about we actually try to do a wheelie, as they say.

2411
02:39:57,220 --> 02:39:58,080
How big is this?

2412
02:39:58,740 --> 02:39:59,800
It's not that big.

2413
02:40:00,940 --> 02:40:01,780
What about that one?

2414
02:40:02,100 --> 02:40:03,420
Oh, these look really cool, though.

2415
02:40:08,300 --> 02:40:14,940
Wait, so, if we're doing that, we can't have... Mark 1 inline cockpit.

2416
02:40:17,700 --> 02:40:19,380
A Rovemate, maybe?

2417
02:40:19,540 --> 02:40:20,000
Oh my god.

2418
02:40:22,040 --> 02:40:23,820
This is way bigger than I expected.

2419
02:40:25,100 --> 02:40:25,980
Jesus Christ.

2420
02:40:29,920 --> 02:40:31,100
Can I change look?

2421
02:40:31,780 --> 02:40:32,380
Oh!

2422
02:40:34,020 --> 02:40:35,060
Oh my god.

2423
02:40:36,360 --> 02:40:37,500
That looks beautiful.

2424
02:40:43,840 --> 02:40:44,620
Rover mate.

2425
02:40:46,060 --> 02:40:47,040
You know what, guys?

2426
02:40:47,060 --> 02:40:48,280
We're doing a rover mate.

2427
02:40:50,140 --> 02:40:50,880
Rover mate.

2428
02:40:54,100 --> 02:40:55,160
Uh... Atheists.

2429
02:40:55,600 --> 02:40:56,660
That was terrible.

2430
02:40:57,300 --> 02:40:59,820
I meant to do, like, a checkmate joke, you know?

2431
02:41:01,320 --> 02:41:02,360
You know what I mean?

2432
02:41:02,540 --> 02:41:04,260
Why do I have a shield on that?

2433
02:41:04,560 --> 02:41:05,800
Wait, what am I actually smoking?

2434
02:41:06,340 --> 02:41:07,400
What was the point of that?

2435
02:41:11,350 --> 02:41:12,470
Get rid of that shit.

2436
02:41:14,430 --> 02:41:14,830
Hello?

2437
02:41:16,390 --> 02:41:21,150
Okay, so all of this needs to be... deleted, I guess.

2438
02:41:21,390 --> 02:41:24,770
We don't... we don't want this.

2439
02:41:26,530 --> 02:41:27,750
I knew that was gonna happen.

2440
02:41:28,370 --> 02:41:29,170
So what do I do?

2441
02:41:30,250 --> 02:41:31,070
Do I do this?

2442
02:41:32,410 --> 02:41:33,150
A new one.

2443
02:41:35,070 --> 02:41:36,010
Get rid of that one.

2444
02:41:36,370 --> 02:41:37,550
The system's a little weird.

2445
02:41:42,650 --> 02:41:43,710
Get rid of that one.

2446
02:41:44,350 --> 02:41:45,570
Now, let's see here.

2447
02:41:46,650 --> 02:41:47,670
Add some wheels!

2448
02:41:51,030 --> 02:41:57,130
I want... Then again, these wheels look like the ones that, you know, the astronauts were driving around in.

2449
02:41:58,070 --> 02:42:01,490
This is more like a car wheel and not a rover wheel, you know what I mean?

2450
02:42:01,750 --> 02:42:02,990
Now, this is called RoveMax.

2451
02:42:09,680 --> 02:42:10,320
Calm down.

2452
02:42:12,060 --> 02:42:13,060
That's more like it.

2453
02:42:18,040 --> 02:42:19,360
Do we have to do it like that?

2454
02:42:19,980 --> 02:42:20,880
