3817
04:15:36,690 --> 04:15:37,690
Beep, beep, beep, beep.

3818
04:15:40,010 --> 04:15:41,050
Run analysis.

3819
04:15:42,970 --> 04:15:45,490
Resource analysis performed for Duna Highlands.

3820
04:15:47,730 --> 04:15:49,490
We've got latitude and longitude.

3821
04:15:50,750 --> 04:15:52,630
Biome Highlands, body Duna.

3822
04:15:53,410 --> 04:15:55,750
Or surf 0%.

3823
04:15:55,750 --> 04:15:56,430
Alright.

3824
04:15:57,050 --> 04:16:00,270
Maybe I can use that in conjunction with the satellite thingy.

3825
04:16:00,910 --> 04:16:01,310
Right?

3826
04:16:01,530 --> 04:16:02,110
Isn't that what it said?

3827
04:16:03,670 --> 04:16:04,730
So this one I already did.

3828
04:16:05,110 --> 04:16:05,990
Can we send this?

3829
04:16:07,190 --> 04:16:07,630
Transmit it.

3830
04:16:12,310 --> 04:16:14,150
It's gonna use up all the battery, but that's okay.

3831
04:16:18,020 --> 04:16:18,440
Done.

3832
04:16:18,680 --> 04:16:19,020
Sent.

3833
04:16:20,140 --> 04:16:21,080
What about temperature?

3834
04:16:22,360 --> 04:16:23,860
Did I forget the temperature sensor?

3835
04:16:24,200 --> 04:16:25,580
There's no way I forgot thermometer.

3836
04:16:27,960 --> 04:16:28,380
Really?

3837
04:16:30,280 --> 04:16:31,060
Oh, there it is.

3838
04:16:31,120 --> 04:16:31,660
It's hidden in there.

3839
04:16:31,740 --> 04:16:33,140
Look, it's in the fucking thing.

3840
04:16:35,520 --> 04:16:38,600
I can't click it, though, because it's being obstructed by this thing.

3841
04:16:43,840 --> 04:16:45,060
What if I do that?

3842
04:16:50,320 --> 04:16:51,480
I may not be able to click that.

3843
04:16:51,620 --> 04:16:52,340
I fucked up on that.

3844
04:16:52,420 --> 04:16:52,820
That's on me.

3845
04:16:55,780 --> 04:16:56,760
It is what it is.

3846
04:16:58,020 --> 04:16:58,840
That's on me.

3847
04:16:59,400 --> 04:17:00,340
Now, this arm, though.

3848
04:17:01,780 --> 04:17:02,940
Let's go find a rock.

3849
04:17:06,240 --> 04:17:06,720
Blueberries?

3850
04:17:08,860 --> 04:17:09,740
Say what?

3851
04:17:11,220 --> 04:17:12,440
Hold up, I'm hungry.

3852
04:17:13,500 --> 04:17:14,620
We're getting blueberries.

3853
04:17:16,760 --> 04:17:17,860
Let's check that out.

3854
04:17:19,320 --> 04:17:20,620
I want to see what that's about.

3855
04:17:24,640 --> 04:17:25,740
Get up there, get up there.

3856
04:17:28,460 --> 04:17:29,500
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

3857
04:17:30,080 --> 04:17:31,700
I want to get blueberries.

3858
04:17:33,640 --> 04:17:34,500
Blueberry muffins.

3859
04:17:35,320 --> 04:17:37,000
That's what's going to happen on Doona later.

3860
04:17:37,460 --> 04:17:38,600
And you're all invited.

3861
04:17:39,680 --> 04:17:40,980
It's going to be a heck of a party.

3862
04:17:44,980 --> 04:17:46,320
These blueberries look red.

3863
04:17:49,340 --> 04:17:50,460
Why are they lying to me?

3864
04:17:54,090 --> 04:17:55,130
What the hell is that?

3865
04:17:55,430 --> 04:17:56,250
That's not a blueberry.

3866
04:17:58,850 --> 04:18:00,310
These kerbals are colorblind.

3867
04:18:01,770 --> 04:18:02,770
Let me try this.

3868
04:18:04,910 --> 04:18:05,730
Scant blueberries!

3869
04:18:07,130 --> 04:18:08,750
Not enough electric char... Oh, okay.

3870
04:18:09,190 --> 04:18:10,330
Let's just charge up, then.

3871
04:18:11,090 --> 04:18:12,090
Where's the sun, anyway?

3872
04:18:13,330 --> 04:18:14,530
Oh, it's right above us.

3873
04:18:14,530 --> 04:18:15,190
That's actually perfect.

3874
04:18:20,520 --> 04:18:22,060
Let's just speed up time here.

3875
04:18:23,160 --> 04:18:24,700
Get a bunch of charge.

3876
04:18:25,340 --> 04:18:27,640
Could have maybe had more batteries on this thing.

3877
04:18:29,880 --> 04:18:30,700
There we go.

3878
04:18:31,880 --> 04:18:32,560
Scan it.

3879
04:18:42,760 --> 04:18:43,720
Oh, cool!

3880
04:18:45,120 --> 04:18:46,180
The little light.

3881
04:18:47,920 --> 04:18:48,980
Oh my god.

3882
04:18:52,740 --> 04:18:55,700
How these formed is still a mystery to scientists back on Kerben.

3883
04:18:56,180 --> 04:18:59,060
Do they have any relationship to the pancake domes on Eve?

3884
04:18:59,440 --> 04:19:03,240
Or is that just a galactic and gastronomical mystery we have yet to solve?

3885
04:19:03,820 --> 04:19:06,520
Who knows where we may find an elusive syrup sample?

3886
04:19:07,440 --> 04:19:10,420
Your scan has collected some, but not all the information available.

3887
04:19:11,020 --> 04:19:12,540
Come back later with a better sensor.

3888
04:19:13,340 --> 04:19:15,480
Aha, so that's probably the medium arm.

3889
04:19:17,360 --> 04:19:17,800
Transmit.

3890
04:19:21,210 --> 04:19:22,190
Did we do it?

3891
04:19:25,950 --> 04:19:26,570
Transmit.

3892
04:19:28,590 --> 04:19:29,410
Transmit data.

3893
04:19:30,270 --> 04:19:31,370
Unable to transmit.

3894
04:19:32,450 --> 04:19:33,810
Ah, we have no connection!

3895
04:19:34,650 --> 04:19:38,270
Ah, Duna lander relay is gone, I see.

3896
04:19:38,790 --> 04:19:39,630
We gotta wait.

3897
04:19:41,230 --> 04:19:42,350
Come back around.

3898
04:19:43,010 --> 04:19:43,970
I need you.

3899
04:19:45,030 --> 04:19:47,070
In fact, we're moving into the Terminator here.

3900
04:19:51,370 --> 04:19:52,130
There we go.

3901
04:19:52,250 --> 04:19:52,970
That should be good enough.

3902
04:19:54,410 --> 04:19:55,210
Oh, pretty.

3903
04:19:55,390 --> 04:19:55,810
Look at this.

3904
04:19:57,110 --> 04:20:01,010
Now, since we have a connection, send it back to Kerbin.

3905
04:20:02,630 --> 04:20:03,370
Transmit all.

3906
04:20:04,710 --> 04:20:05,650
Whatever I have.

3907
04:20:05,950 --> 04:20:06,890
Just send it.

3908
04:20:10,930 --> 04:20:12,130
Oh, yeah, we're sending a lot.

3909
04:20:13,630 --> 04:20:15,190
That's a lot of battery being used.

3910
04:20:17,070 --> 04:20:17,510
Yeah.

3911
04:20:18,030 --> 04:20:18,510
Any more?

3912
04:20:18,750 --> 04:20:19,450
Oh, there's more!

3913
04:20:20,750 --> 04:20:21,370
Oh, shit.

3914
04:20:22,030 --> 04:20:22,970
Okay, any more?

3915
04:20:23,970 --> 04:20:24,410
Oh!

3916
04:20:24,790 --> 04:20:25,930
Not enough electric charge.

3917
04:20:26,030 --> 04:20:27,210
Okay, then I'm just gonna wait a bit.

3918
04:20:31,860 --> 04:20:32,920
Oh, the sun is set.

3919
04:20:35,760 --> 04:20:37,640
Oh, we're losing battery now.

3920
04:20:38,600 --> 04:20:40,600
Turn off the screen to save some power, I guess.

3921
04:20:43,640 --> 04:20:45,400
How are we spending power right now?

3922
04:20:46,660 --> 04:20:47,380
What's running?

3923
04:20:47,880 --> 04:20:48,780
Is it the brakes?

3924
04:20:50,320 --> 04:20:51,280
No, turn them back on.

3925
04:20:52,600 --> 04:20:53,860
It may have been the brakes.

3926
04:20:54,680 --> 04:20:58,800
What is causing this thing to... What is draining power?

3927
04:21:00,620 --> 04:21:02,320
Can I go like hibernation?

3928
04:21:04,080 --> 04:21:04,760
There we go.

3929
04:21:04,860 --> 04:21:06,320
Hibernate while the sun is down?

3930
04:21:15,630 --> 04:21:16,550
Night on Doona.

3931
04:21:17,090 --> 04:21:18,390
Oh, and the Milky Way comes out.

3932
04:21:19,410 --> 04:21:20,210
Look at that.

3933
04:21:21,610 --> 04:21:22,890
If only I had a little light.

3934
04:21:23,030 --> 04:21:24,930
I should have put a light on the fucking rover.

3935
04:21:28,410 --> 04:21:28,850
Wow.

3936
04:21:30,570 --> 04:21:31,890
Tell me that isn't cool.

3937
04:21:34,810 --> 04:21:35,930
It's a little dark, though.

3938
04:21:52,990 --> 04:21:53,730
Where's the sun?

3939
04:21:53,870 --> 04:21:54,550
Oh, here it comes!

3940
04:21:57,910 --> 04:21:58,990
From that side, of course.

3941
04:22:00,270 --> 04:22:01,150
Oh, wow.

3942
04:22:02,650 --> 04:22:04,650
Okay, we got electric charge again.

3943
04:22:05,570 --> 04:22:06,270
Keep sending.

3944
04:22:09,570 --> 04:22:12,890
Yo, this take... Hold on, we need to allow partial.

3945
04:22:17,530 --> 04:22:18,350
Allow partial.

3946
04:22:18,450 --> 04:22:19,350
Let me just fast forward here.

3947
04:22:24,350 --> 04:22:26,030
Not enough electric... Oh, what, what?

3948
04:22:26,210 --> 04:22:26,890
Is it not sending?

3949
04:22:29,650 --> 04:22:31,330
No, it was sent, it was sent.

3950
04:22:31,810 --> 04:22:32,790
It's still sending, though.

3951
04:22:36,790 --> 04:22:37,810
56% now.

3952
04:22:39,730 --> 04:22:40,970
Just keep fast-forwarding.

3953
04:22:42,210 --> 04:22:43,450
There we go, 100%.

3954
04:22:43,450 --> 04:22:45,230
Chemutron 16, done.

3955
04:22:45,330 --> 04:22:46,490
There we go, we sent it all.

3956
04:22:47,630 --> 04:22:50,730
The data has been acquired from the surface of Duna.

3957
04:22:58,080 --> 04:22:59,320
I'm gonna turn around here.

3958
04:22:59,840 --> 04:23:04,860
I'm actually gonna get down to the flat area again before I leave this, because I'm afraid of this thing rolling down somehow.

3959
04:23:06,060 --> 04:23:07,120
Wait, I have no authority!

3960
04:23:07,240 --> 04:23:07,660
I have no authority!

3961
04:23:07,880 --> 04:23:08,600
Why, why, why?

3962
04:23:09,040 --> 04:23:09,880
Oh, I got no connection.

3963
04:23:10,480 --> 04:23:11,740
Break, break, break, break, break, break.

3964
04:23:13,420 --> 04:23:14,980
Aw, you asshole, come back.

3965
04:23:16,280 --> 04:23:17,200
I'm gonna wait for it.

3966
04:23:20,250 --> 04:23:21,350
And connection.

3967
04:23:24,730 --> 04:23:27,230
Now... Brakes off.

3968
04:23:29,630 --> 04:23:31,850
I still can't control.

3969
04:23:33,250 --> 04:23:34,430
Brake, brake, brake.

3970
04:23:34,750 --> 04:23:35,850
Why can't I control it?

3971
04:23:39,370 --> 04:23:40,670
Electric charge.

3972
04:23:41,790 --> 04:23:43,530
It's like the wheels are not responding.

3973
04:23:45,130 --> 04:23:46,310
Why is that?

3974
04:23:49,150 --> 04:23:50,690
Oh, it's hibernating!

3975
04:23:50,930 --> 04:23:51,870
That's why.

3976
04:25:00,890 --> 04:25:03,330
If you hadn't guessed it, this is the end screen.

3977
04:25:18,430 --> 04:25:19,210
We made it.

3978
04:25:26,050 --> 04:25:27,210
We made it to Duna.

3979
04:25:30,570 --> 04:25:31,830
What do you think about that, guys?

3980
04:25:34,210 --> 04:25:35,290
That's the end of the stream.

3981
04:25:40,870 --> 04:25:43,630
I can't believe everything came together like that at the end.

3982
04:25:45,370 --> 04:25:56,150
I don't know if you noticed, but... the voice in that song just now... I adjusted that... in, like, audio editing... to make it sound like a Kerbal.

3983
04:26:01,020 --> 04:26:03,000
I was hoping that song would come on today.

3984
04:26:08,050 --> 04:26:10,890
Man, can you believe that we went to Mars?

3985
04:26:13,010 --> 04:26:18,590
I feel like I had so many moments of utter despair on my way here.

3986
04:26:19,190 --> 04:26:24,670
So many moments where I thought, oh, I forgot that this was a thing, now I know I can't do it.

3987
04:26:24,990 --> 04:26:29,170
And we somehow managed to land despite all odds.

3988
04:26:31,310 --> 04:26:31,870
Incredible.

3989
04:26:38,200 --> 04:26:40,280
I'm just sitting here smiling like an idiot.

3990
04:26:40,500 --> 04:26:43,200
This is just... something else, isn't it?

3991
04:26:43,660 --> 04:26:46,400
What other game out there can give you something like this?

3992
04:26:47,440 --> 04:26:49,960
The answer is... no other game, I don't think.

3993
04:26:51,920 --> 04:26:54,620
Now, I haven't played every game, but... I'm pretty sure.

3994
04:26:57,040 --> 04:26:57,520
Incredible.

3995
04:27:02,330 --> 04:27:04,310
Oh, I did not try free IVA again.

3996
04:27:05,050 --> 04:27:05,790
I forgot.

3997
04:27:06,190 --> 04:27:07,190
I'm sorry, I forgot.

3998
04:27:11,210 --> 04:27:15,850
At this point, I'm convinced you're running a many-worlds experiment, and we're seeing your winning universe.

3999
04:27:18,490 --> 04:27:19,910
It's actually much simpler than that.

4000
04:27:20,070 --> 04:27:20,910
This is just a recording.

4001
04:27:21,330 --> 04:27:22,610
This took 100 takes.

4002
04:27:23,010 --> 04:27:24,410
This is just the one that works.

4003
04:27:28,350 --> 04:27:29,150
How you so good?

4004
04:27:29,250 --> 04:27:30,190
I was born like it, man.

4005
04:27:30,330 --> 04:27:30,770
What can I say?

4006
04:27:31,750 --> 04:27:33,770
Now, I've had my fair share of failures, okay?

4007
04:27:38,530 --> 04:27:39,830
You know what I love?

4008
04:27:39,930 --> 04:27:42,230
I love it when there's more doubters than believers.

4009
04:27:42,670 --> 04:27:44,190
Because that fuels me even more.

4010
04:27:44,330 --> 04:27:45,550
I'm like, oh, I'm going to show these fuckers.

4011
04:27:45,610 --> 04:27:46,190
They don't believe in me?

4012
04:27:46,270 --> 04:27:47,290
They don't believe I can do this?

4013
04:27:48,570 --> 04:27:49,530
Oh, I'll show you.

4014
04:27:54,020 --> 04:27:57,860
I think if everyone was like, yeah, you can do it, then I would probably be complacent.

4015
04:27:58,160 --> 04:27:59,480
And I would do stupid mistakes.

4016
04:28:03,050 --> 04:28:06,190
I really thought we were gonna crash at the end there when the parachutes didn't come on.

4017
04:28:07,770 --> 04:28:10,750
Like... That was way too close for comfort.

4018
04:28:13,570 --> 04:28:15,670
We thought you had no chance without a power of descent.

4019
04:28:15,730 --> 04:28:16,470
That's what I thought.

4020
04:28:17,170 --> 04:28:22,630
Especially when I came into the atmosphere at first and I was like at 30 kilometers and I was not slowing down.

4021
04:28:23,310 --> 04:28:26,070
At that point, I was like, okay, this atmosphere is too thin.

4022
04:28:26,510 --> 04:28:27,510
I cannot slow down.

4023
04:28:27,630 --> 04:28:28,550
My parachutes are useless.

4024
04:28:29,090 --> 04:28:30,010
This heat shield does nothing.

4025
04:28:30,760 --> 04:28:31,580
That's what I thought.

4026
04:28:36,640 --> 04:28:37,840
I'm glad we made it, though.

4027
04:28:41,100 --> 04:28:41,900
Unbelievable end.

4028
04:28:46,400 --> 04:28:48,300
Man, this is such a good shot, man.

4029
04:28:48,540 --> 04:28:49,660
Like, Duna is beautiful.

4030
04:28:50,740 --> 04:28:51,320
Isn't it?

4031
04:28:52,460 --> 04:28:53,300
What a planet.

4032
04:28:54,760 --> 04:28:56,520
I mean, it is exactly what I expected.

4033
04:28:57,740 --> 04:28:59,460
But hey, still pretty.

4034
04:29:07,880 --> 04:29:09,660
Maybe make a different chat for this end screen.

4035
04:29:10,540 --> 04:29:11,900
Yeah, I guess I could do that.

4036
04:29:14,420 --> 04:29:17,600
But, I mean... I don't know what I'm gonna end up with, right?

4037
04:29:17,720 --> 04:29:20,060
This is just, like, improvised end screen, I guess.

4038
04:29:23,690 --> 04:29:26,490
What a fantastic session here of gaming.

4039
04:29:27,310 --> 04:29:29,130
Man, this really hits the spot.

4040
04:29:31,550 --> 04:29:32,790
Like, I'm fulfilled.

4041
04:29:32,990 --> 04:29:34,330
In this moment, I'm happy, you know?

4042
04:29:34,910 --> 04:29:36,710
That was freaking great.

4043
04:29:40,600 --> 04:29:49,200
Also, remember when I was trying to burn towards Duna, and it took like 3,500 delta V, and I was like, oh, this may not happen, huh?

4044
04:29:49,960 --> 04:29:55,240
And then somehow, I managed to get there with a thousand, like, pinpoint precision.

4045
04:29:56,040 --> 04:29:58,360
I have no idea how that even happened.

4046
04:29:59,920 --> 04:30:02,000
That was like pure luck, I think.

4047
04:30:02,740 --> 04:30:04,000
With a little bit of skill.

4048
04:30:04,700 --> 04:30:07,360
Maybe 75% luck, 25% skill.

4049
04:30:08,390 --> 04:30:11,710
And a little bit of extra power of will.

4050
04:30:25,990 --> 04:30:26,430
Yo.

4051
04:30:26,430 --> 04:30:27,870
I would love to do that.

4052
04:30:28,010 --> 04:30:30,390
The problem is, that music is copyrighted.

4053
04:30:31,050 --> 04:30:34,210
It is a very strong idea, and I support it fully.

4054
04:30:36,190 --> 04:30:40,050
And then the sound of, like, you know, the camera... You know, when you do a trick?

4055
04:30:40,810 --> 04:30:41,250
Yeah.

4056
04:30:47,340 --> 04:30:48,020
Sound effect.

4057
04:30:48,200 --> 04:30:51,000
Yeah, sound... Okay, I guess sound effects could be kind of fun.

4058
04:30:51,500 --> 04:30:58,240
So whenever a rocket spins or, like, does a trick, then it's like... That could be quite fun, actually.

4059
04:30:58,600 --> 04:30:59,520
That's a good idea.

4060
04:31:00,600 --> 04:31:01,660
An orchestra hit.

4061
04:31:03,900 --> 04:31:04,540
You know what?

4062
04:31:04,540 --> 04:31:06,520
I was thinking maybe I should have, like, soundboard stuff.

4063
04:31:07,080 --> 04:31:09,500
For example, the, you know, the trailer boom.

4064
04:31:09,880 --> 04:31:11,060
When something goes wrong.

4065
04:31:13,980 --> 04:31:15,340
I forgot what the name of that one is.

4066
04:31:15,380 --> 04:31:16,420
But, like, something like that.

4067
04:31:16,480 --> 04:31:18,220
I think it could add some fun elements to this.

4068
04:31:20,520 --> 04:31:20,920
Rampage.

4069
04:31:22,140 --> 04:31:24,980
That would only make sense if kerbals are dying en masse.

4070
04:31:25,660 --> 04:31:27,860
Imagine just falling from the sky with no parachutes.

4071
04:31:28,200 --> 04:31:30,740
One splashes into the ground into a red mist.

4072
04:31:31,140 --> 04:31:32,680
I guess it would be a green mist.

4073
04:31:33,280 --> 04:31:35,460
And then, like, double kill.

4074
04:31:36,260 --> 04:31:37,160
Triple kill.

4075
04:31:39,820 --> 04:31:40,520
That's horrible.

4076
04:31:42,230 --> 04:31:43,750
Have you tried to build planes yet?

4077
04:31:43,850 --> 04:31:44,450
I have not.

4078
04:31:44,950 --> 04:31:46,090
